Title: Window size and position requests take effect
Repository: SDL 3.4.12 with contrib SDL3-3.4.12-aros.diff (contrib 142b3ff4)
Date: 2026-11-20
Author: aros-sdl project
Problem: SDL3 keeps a requested size or position in window->pending until the backend reports it; window->x/y/w/h still hold the old values when the backend is called. The AROS backend read the old values, so SDL_SetWindowSize asked Intuition for the size the window already had, and SDL_SetWindowPosition for the old position together with the size Intuition showed at that moment, which undid a resize still in flight. A position left of or above the screen (a centred window larger than the screen) was passed on and put the title bar out of reach. There was no SyncWindow, so a program could not wait for the result, and no usable display bounds, so a program could not tell how much room a window has.
Change: Both calls ask Intuition for one box made of the pending values and, for the rest, of the window's current ones. A requested position is moved so that the window starts on the screen, below the screen bar. Requests are counted, and the IDCMP_CHANGEWINDOW that answers the last one ends a pending request also when nothing changed. SDL_SyncWindow waits up to 500 ms for Intuition to apply the request. SDL_GetDisplayUsableBounds returns the screen without the screen bar.
Scope: AROS (src/video/aros)
Upstream: candidate (aros-development-team/contrib SDL3); not sent while contrib PRs 89 to 92 are open, they change the same sections of contrib's diff
Verification: kits build for mainline x86_64, Raspberry Pi and x86_64 ABIv11. Mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15, 800x600 Workbench screen), 2026-11-20, LOVE 12.0 with OpenGL: before, SDL_SetWindowSize(640, 360) left a 780x565 window as it was, and a centred window asked for at 1280x720 opened 240 pixels left of the screen; after, the same request gives a 640x360 window, a following 729x547 request is applied, SDL_SyncWindow returns with the new size in SDL_GetWindowSize, and the windows start on the screen below the screen bar. Not run: Raspberry Pi and ABIv11, a custom screen, borderless windows.
Removal: when contrib reads window->pending in these calls
